"use strict";(self.webpackChunktranzila_payment_for_woocommerce_pos_doc=self.webpackChunktranzila_payment_for_woocommerce_pos_doc||[]).push([[235],{2124(e,t,a){a.r(t),a.d(t,{_pageData:()=>i,default:()=>r});var n=a(641);const i=JSON.parse('{"path":"/tranzila-payment/admin-configuration.html","title":"Admin Configuration","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"tranzila-payment/admin-configuration.md"}'),o={name:"admin-configuration.md"},r=(0,a(6262).A)(o,[["render",function(e,t,a,i,o,r){return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="admin-configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-configuration"><span>Admin Configuration</span></a></h1><p>Configure the WooCommerce POS gateway settings and map physical credit card terminals to specific retail locations to begin accepting cards via Tranzila.</p><hr><div id="payment-gateway-setup"></div><h2 id="_1-pos-payment-gateway-setup" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-pos-payment-gateway-setup"><span>1. POS Payment Gateway Setup</span></a></h2><p>To register and activate the Tranzila payment gateway globally inside your Point of Sale dashboard, navigate to <strong>Point of Sale → Settings</strong> and select the <strong>Payment</strong> tab.</p><h3 id="payment-methods-list" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#payment-methods-list"><span>Payment Methods List</span></a></h3><p>This screen lists all available payment options for your cashiers. Ensure that <strong>Tranzila Terminal</strong> is active.</p><p><img src="/tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos/images/tranzila-payment/payment-methods-list.png" alt="Payment Methods List"></p><h3 id="editing-gateway-metadata" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#editing-gateway-metadata"><span>Editing Gateway Metadata</span></a></h3><p>Click <strong>Edit</strong> next to the Tranzila Terminal entry to customize the checkout drawer display details for your cashiers:</p><p><img src="/tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos/images/tranzila-payment/payment-gateway-configuration.png" alt="Payment Gateway Configuration"></p><ul><li><em><em>Payment Name</em>:</em>* The cashier-facing label displayed in the POS payment drawer during checkout (e.g. <code>Tranzila Terminal</code> or <code>Card Terminal</code>).</li><li><em><em>Payment Slug</em>:</em>* Unique system identifier used internally by WooCommerce POS (default: <code>wcpos_tranzila</code>).</li><li><em><em>Payment Description</em>:</em>* The instructions displayed beneath the payment name (e.g. <code>Tranzila Payment Terminal gateway</code>).</li><li><em><em>Status</em>:</em>* Set this to <strong>Enable</strong> to make the option selectable at checkouts.</li><li><strong>Update Payment:</strong> Click this button to save and apply your custom label updates.</li></ul><hr><div id="tranzila-terminal-settings"></div><h2 id="_2-outlet-terminal-configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-outlet-terminal-configuration"><span>2. Outlet Terminal Configuration</span></a></h2><p>Tranzila terminal credentials must be configured for each retail location (Outlet) individually to ensure sales are routed to the appropriate merchant accounts.</p><p>Navigate to <strong>Point of Sale → Outlets</strong>, click <strong>Edit</strong> on your desired outlet, and scroll down to the <strong>Payment Options</strong> section. Check <strong>Tranzila Terminal</strong> to reveal the terminal-specific settings fields:</p><p><img src="/tranzila-payment-for-woocommerce-pos/images/tranzila-payment/outlet-configuration.png" alt="Tranzila Outlet Settings"></p><h3 id="configuration-fields" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#configuration-fields"><span>Configuration Fields</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>POS ID:</strong> The unique terminal identifier assigned to your physical card reader by Tranzila. This value is usually printed on the terminal hardware sticker or merchant contract.</li><li><strong>Supplier Name:</strong> The merchant supplier identifier registered with your Tranzila merchant account (default sandbox supplier is <code>tranzilap</code>).</li><li><strong>Company Name:</strong> The merchant legal business name or shop name that will be displayed on customer credit card slips and receipts.</li><li><strong>Transaction Mode:</strong> Controls the transaction destination environment: <ul><li><strong>Sandbox:</strong> Redirects requests to Tranzila&#39;s testing servers for mock transaction verifications.</li><li><strong>Production:</strong> Routes payments to Tranzila&#39;s live transaction network to capture real money charges.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Credit Type:</strong> Select the credit processing method to support: <ul><li><em>Regular Credit (Standard credit card single charges)</em></li><li><em>Payments (Installments or payment splitting)</em></li></ul></li></ul><hr><h2 id="_3-saving-configurations" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-saving-configurations"><span>3. Saving Configurations</span></a></h2><p>After configuring terminal settings:</p><ol><li>Click <strong>Save Configurations</strong> at the bottom of the POS Settings screen to store gateway descriptions.</li><li>Click <strong>Update</strong> on the POS Outlets edit screen to persist terminal IDs and Supplier keys.</li><li>Reload your POS register screen to download the updated configuration files.</li></ol><blockquote><p>[!IMPORTANT] <strong>Outlet-Specific Isolation:</strong> If you have multiple outlets, you <strong>must</strong> configure these settings for each outlet profile individually. Cashiers logging into Outlet A will not have access to terminal details configured for Outlet B.</p></blockquote>',26)])])}]])}}]);